{"name":"Night Flight","hex":"#434d5c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"flight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of flying; the ability to fly.","An instance of flying."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fast, swift, fleet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red-eye flight","blocks":[{"text":"In commercial aviation, a red-eye flight refers to a flight that departs at night and arrives the next morning, especially when the total flight time is insufficient for passengers to get a full night's sleep."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/SU-GEW_08062019LHR_%2848940694778%29.jpg/330px-SU-GEW_08062019LHR_%2848940694778%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red-eye_flight","wikidata":"Q1363305"},{"title":"Night Flight (Yvonne Elliman album)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Flight is a 1978 album by Yvonne Elliman featuring the number-one song \"If I Can't Have You\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Night_Flight_%28Yvonne_Elliman_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Flight_(Yvonne_Elliman_album)","wikidata":"Q131516173"},{"title":"Night Flight (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Flight is an eclectic variety television show that originated on cable TV network USA Network."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Night-Flight-TV-series-title-screen.jpg/330px-Night-Flight-TV-series-title-screen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Flight_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q17071792"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Variable spellings of night in a Middle English poem:\n\nÞu sittest a dai & fliȝst a niȝt (top)\nÞu sittest a day and flyhst a niht (bottom)\n'You sit by day and fly by night'\n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOwl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c